WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.603 --> 00:00:06.667
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

00:00:07.407 --> 00:00:09.996
[wind howls]
Hey, it's getting kind of drafty in here.

00:00:09.996 --> 00:00:12.045
[wind howls]
I can barely hear myself think.

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:14.096
[wind howls]

00:00:14.096 --> 00:00:16.573
[wind howls]
Oh, yeah, that's a breeze all right.

00:00:16.573 --> 00:00:18.399
[wind howls]
I wonder how far I can make my spit go

00:00:18.399 --> 00:00:20.273
[wind howls]
if I was to hock a loogie into the...

00:00:20.273 --> 00:00:21.690
[wind howls]
no, better not.

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:22.930
[wind howls]
Too bad the bodies landed on the

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:24.595
[wind howls]
other side of the door,

00:00:24.595 --> 00:00:25.801
[wind howls]
then I could just toss them in and

00:00:25.801 --> 00:00:27.806
[wind howls]
watch them explode.

00:00:27.806 --> 00:00:29.963
[wind howls]
COME ON! THIS IS STUPID!

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:32.278
[wind howls]
Huh? What about the keypad?

00:00:32.278 --> 00:00:33.250
[wind howls]
Yeah!

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:34.605
[wind howls]
WAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA--

00:00:34.605 --> 00:00:35.563
[wind howls]
OOF!

00:00:35.563 --> 00:00:39.637
[wind howls]
[ragged coughing]

00:00:39.637 --> 00:00:41.127
[wind howls]
[wheeze]

00:00:41.127 --> 00:00:43.048
[wind howls]
[raspy voice] How is this happening...?

00:00:43.048 --> 00:00:44.749
[wind howls]
[raspy voice] Just let me out of here...

00:00:44.749 --> 00:00:46.359
[wind howls]

00:00:46.359 --> 00:00:47.746
[wind howls]
[raspy voice] Jesus Christ...

00:00:47.746 --> 00:00:49.179
[wind howls]
[raspy voice] This must be a windspeed

00:00:49.179 --> 00:00:51.647
[wind howls]
[raspy voice] of 150 miles an hour...

00:00:51.647 --> 00:00:54.604
[wind howls]
[raspy voice] Stop persecuting me...

00:00:54.604 --> 00:00:55.727
[wind howls]
[raspy voice] all of you...

00:00:55.727 --> 00:00:56.403
[wind howls]

00:00:56.403 --> 00:00:58.667
[wind howls]
[raspy voice] Stop... stop...

00:01:01.214 --> 00:01:04.000
[raspy voice] I guess now I know
why that door wouldn't open.

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:08.603
[raspy voice] That must be why
those boards were up there, too.

00:01:08.603 --> 00:01:09.567
[raspy voice] Shhh.

00:01:10.485 --> 00:01:13.019
[raspy voice] This must've
happened before.

00:01:13.019 --> 00:01:16.065
[raspy voice] I bet they used to
have it lined with spikes.

00:01:16.065 --> 00:01:20.000
[raspy voice] Then, one day they came in
and found the janitor impaled on the ceiling.

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:25.666
[raspy voice] I mean, my God, I'm not
even wearing air-resistant clothing.

00:01:25.666 --> 00:01:29.202
[raspy voice] I thought you had to be
wearing MC Hammer pants and a poncho

00:01:29.202 --> 00:01:30.498
[raspy voice] for that to work.

00:01:30.498 --> 00:01:32.868
[raspy voice] You don't deal
with this in theoretical physics.

00:01:34.591 --> 00:01:36.041
[raspy voice] It's just numbers,

00:01:36.041 --> 00:01:38.854
but rocket scientists don't
have that excuse.

00:01:38.854 --> 00:01:40.390
They have to test the rockets,

00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:42.479
no matter how many people get killed.

00:01:42.479 --> 00:01:43.868
But I respect that.

00:01:44.698 --> 00:01:45.634
You know?

00:01:47.118 --> 00:01:47.634
Huh?!

00:01:48.697 --> 00:01:51.326
DO YOU PEOPLE HEAR ANYTHING I'M SAYING?!

00:01:51.326 --> 00:01:52.968
I DON'T THINK YOU DO!

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:55.767
"Oxy"? Is this oxycodone?!

00:01:56.439 --> 00:01:59.228
Oh, no, it's probably just oxygen.

00:01:59.228 --> 00:02:03.133
I don't think you can get high
off oxygen; it just makes you more alert.

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:06.762
I don't really know what I'm
doing, but, y'know,

00:02:06.762 --> 00:02:10.389
pushing buttons and having it do
something is sort of its own reward.

00:02:10.389 --> 00:02:13.837
Not that I don't have better
things to be doing with my time.

00:02:13.837 --> 00:02:17.445
I need to start looking for a new job
and get cracking on that lawsuit.

00:02:17.445 --> 00:02:19.482
I've got shit to do!

00:02:19.482 --> 00:02:22.207
God dammit! This is that door
that wouldn't open!

00:02:22.207 --> 00:02:24.217
I'VE GONE IN CIRCLES AGAIN!

00:02:24.822 --> 00:02:27.250
[growls]

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:29.900
Actually, I don't feel like
looking for a new job.

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:34.120
I want to go on vacation like
Hawaii or some place in the Caribbean.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:38.247
Actually, what I really want is a rebreather
so then I can tame a giant sea turtle

00:02:38.247 --> 00:02:39.656
and learn how to ride it.

00:02:39.656 --> 00:02:42.874
Once I can ride a sea turtle,
that opens up some options.

00:02:42.874 --> 00:02:45.012
Then I can come up on
cruise ships undetected

00:02:45.012 --> 00:02:47.559
and shoot tranquilizer darts
at the passengers.

00:02:47.559 --> 00:02:48.607
That'd be fun.

00:02:48.607 --> 00:02:51.002
Actually, if I had some
ninja claws, I could

00:02:51.002 --> 00:02:53.406
scale... the side... of the boat...

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:56.114
and then come aboard
at night and rob people.

00:02:56.114 --> 00:02:59.229
I mean, y'know a cruise ship
would be loaded with loot.

00:02:59.229 --> 00:03:02.901
And I'd have the perfect
getaway vehicle: my sea turtle.

00:03:02.901 --> 00:03:05.631
Hell, I could get the
vacation to pay for itself.

00:03:05.631 --> 00:03:07.826
[tentacles moan]
I think I'd name the sea turtle "Flippy".

00:03:07.826 --> 00:03:09.692
[tentacles moan]
That's a good gender-neutral name.

00:03:09.692 --> 00:03:11.826
[tentacles moan]
Or maybe I'd call it "Whiskers" as a joke,

00:03:11.826 --> 00:03:13.614
[tentacles moan]
because that's what you'd name a cat.

00:03:13.614 --> 00:03:15.025
[metal banging]
The cruise ship guests would think

00:03:15.025 --> 00:03:16.124
[metal banging]
that's pretty funny until I

00:03:16.124 --> 00:03:17.005
[metal banging]
pulled a gun on them.

00:03:17.005 --> 00:03:17.963
[tentacles moan]

00:03:17.963 --> 00:03:19.809
[metal banging]
Wow, you might be a reptile

00:03:19.809 --> 00:03:21.302
[metal banging]
but you're really dangerous.

00:03:21.302 --> 00:03:23.246
[metal banging]
You're not like a turtle at all.

00:03:23.246 --> 00:03:24.364
[tentacles moan]
I don't like that.

00:03:24.364 --> 00:03:26.923
[tentacles moan]

00:03:26.923 --> 00:03:28.318
[explosion, tentacles moan]

00:03:28.318 --> 00:03:29.246
[metal banging]

00:03:29.246 --> 00:03:30.189
[metal banging]
God, how can this thing

00:03:30.189 --> 00:03:32.205
[metal banging]
just shrug off a grenade?

00:03:32.205 --> 00:03:33.520
[metal banging]
It should kill anything.

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:34.096
[metal banging]

00:03:34.096 --> 00:03:36.400
[metal banging]
God, STOP BANGING! JESUS!

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:39.867
[metal banging]

00:03:39.867 --> 00:03:41.401
[metal banging]
You know, some cultures sacrifice

00:03:41.401 --> 00:03:43.326
[metal banging]
people to volcanoes or whatever.

00:03:43.326 --> 00:03:44.935
[metal banging]
I'd sacrifice people to this thing

00:03:44.935 --> 00:03:46.206
[metal banging]
if it would keep it quiet.

00:03:46.206 --> 00:03:46.742
[tentacles moan]

00:03:46.742 --> 00:03:48.391
[tentacles moan]
Man, now it's blocking the way

00:03:48.391 --> 00:03:49.402
[tentacles moan]
I want to go.

00:03:49.402 --> 00:03:50.379
[metal banging]
I have no sympathy

00:03:50.379 --> 00:03:51.865
[metal banging]
for this thing whatsoever.

00:03:51.865 --> 00:03:56.097
[tentacles moan]

00:03:56.097 --> 00:03:56.570
[metal banging]
God!

00:03:56.570 --> 00:03:57.792
[metal banging]

00:03:57.792 --> 00:03:58.579
[metal banging]
Yeah, that's right!

00:03:58.579 --> 00:04:01.051
[metal banging]
You show that metal floor who's boss!

00:04:01.051 --> 00:04:02.683
[metal banging]
Don't take "no" for an answer!

00:04:02.683 --> 00:04:04.011
[metal banging]

00:04:04.011 --> 00:04:05.892
[metal banging]
Yeah, they'll be handing out

00:04:05.892 --> 00:04:07.928
[metal banging]
defense contracts like candy

00:04:07.928 --> 00:04:09.233
[tentacles moan]
once they see a monster that's

00:04:09.233 --> 00:04:10.838
[tentacles moan]
immune to grenades.

00:04:10.838 --> 00:04:12.186
Money money money.

00:04:12.186 --> 00:04:15.906
Man, between suing Black Mesa
and being in a key field for a new job,

00:04:15.906 --> 00:04:19.434
I might be able to fund building
a robot army like I always wanted to.

00:04:20.184 --> 00:04:22.383
Dammit, I can't jump this!

00:04:22.383 --> 00:04:25.240
Jackie Chan couldn't jump this!

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:29.901
Well, maybe he could if he kicked off
from wall to wall, but I'm not that good.

00:04:30.746 --> 00:04:35.067
Ah, see, if I had a grappling hook,
I could throw it up there and swing across.

00:04:35.796 --> 00:04:36.570
Maybe.

00:04:37.484 --> 00:04:40.334
Maybe it's just as well I don't
have a grappling hook.

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:45.006
Oh, what am I saying?
Of course I want a grappling hook,

00:04:45.006 --> 00:04:47.105
or a harpoon or something.

00:04:47.105 --> 00:04:48.522
Of course, the real problem here is that

00:04:48.522 --> 00:04:51.358
[metal banging]
Earth's gravity is just too damned high.

00:04:51.358 --> 00:04:53.052
See, case in point.

00:04:53.052 --> 00:04:56.112
If I was on Mars, I wouldn't even
have to think about this gap,

00:04:56.112 --> 00:04:57.649
but as it stands, I'm like a monkey

00:04:57.649 --> 00:05:00.604
trying to decide whether he can
reach the next branch or not.

00:05:00.604 --> 00:05:02.792
It's a wonder we've even made it this far.

00:05:02.792 --> 00:05:06.081
We should've all fallen from
trees and be extinct right now.

00:05:06.081 --> 00:05:08.634
Okay, focus. Don't die.

00:05:09.229 --> 00:05:10.707
Don't die.

00:05:10.707 --> 00:05:11.234
Hup!

00:05:12.655 --> 00:05:13.934
[metal banging]
Oh God.

00:05:13.934 --> 00:05:15.639
[metal banging]
Don't want to do that again.

00:05:15.639 --> 00:05:16.838
[metal banging]
This would be more fun if

00:05:16.838 --> 00:05:18.068
[metal banging]
I was an adrenaline-junkie.

00:05:18.068 --> 00:05:19.767
[tentacles roar]
[BANG]

00:05:21.722 --> 00:05:23.955
[metal banging]
Oh, now I know I'm going the right way.

00:05:23.955 --> 00:05:24.861
[tentacles moan]

00:05:24.861 --> 00:05:26.020
[tentacles moan]
Right.

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:27.850
[tentacles moan]

00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:29.304
[tentacles moan]
Jesus Christ...

00:05:29.304 --> 00:05:31.155
[tentacles moan]

00:05:31.155 --> 00:05:32.401
[tentacles moan]
[growls]

00:05:32.401 --> 00:05:34.275
[metal banging]
If you think I won't shoot you in the back

00:05:34.275 --> 00:05:35.016
[metal banging]
you're mistaken.

00:05:35.016 --> 00:05:37.085
[metal banging]

00:05:37.085 --> 00:05:38.792
[metal banging]
Okay, everybody's dead.

00:05:38.792 --> 00:05:40.268
[metal banging]
Just the way I like it.

00:05:40.268 --> 00:05:42.199
[metal banging]
God, my knees are shaking from

00:05:42.199 --> 00:05:44.151
[metal banging]
going across those gaps.

00:05:44.151 --> 00:05:45.264
[metal banging]
You'd think I'd be getting used to

00:05:45.264 --> 00:05:46.813
[metal banging]
doing leaps and edging my way

00:05:46.813 --> 00:05:48.026
[metal banging]
along ledges

00:05:48.026 --> 00:05:51.328
but there's always that chill knowing
that if I make one small mistake,

00:05:51.328 --> 00:05:53.152
I'll be dead within seconds.

00:05:53.152 --> 00:05:55.801
I'm not used to performance
reviews like that.

00:05:56.215 --> 00:06:00.246
Okay, so I should NOT shoot the
gas canisters with a shotgun.

00:06:00.246 --> 00:06:01.534
I think I'm getting it.

00:06:02.172 --> 00:06:06.246
I'm starting to see how someone
could go crazy down here.

00:06:06.246 --> 00:06:08.623
I'm seeing monsters as big as a building,

00:06:08.623 --> 00:06:10.712
ones that teleport out of the air,

00:06:10.712 --> 00:06:12.825
soldiers trying to kill me,

00:06:12.825 --> 00:06:15.283
a giant building with no exits,

00:06:15.283 --> 00:06:16.930
a crazy-o-meter...

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:19.637
But see, now it's kind of
peaceful and quiet,

00:06:19.637 --> 00:06:22.419
and it makes me wonder if I'm
just imagining everything.

00:06:22.419 --> 00:06:25.566
But no matter how sane or
rational I think I am,

00:06:25.566 --> 00:06:27.880
I'M STILL STUCK IN THIS BUILDING!

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:28.768
[houndeyes charging up]

00:06:28.768 --> 00:06:30.388
[houndeyes charging up]
Oh. Good.

00:06:30.388 --> 00:06:30.920
[houndeyes charging up]
Perfect.

00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:31.839
[sonic boom]

00:06:31.839 --> 00:06:34.100
[houndeye chirruping]
Yeah, see, this is what I'm talking about.

00:06:35.138 --> 00:06:39.195
Everything's fine then chirping maggots
with legs start popping around the corner.

00:06:39.195 --> 00:06:42.647
That's crazy. I'm not crazy
and I know that's crazy.

00:06:42.647 --> 00:06:44.660
[bullsquid moans]

00:06:44.660 --> 00:06:46.982
Yeah, that's right, moan!  MOAN!

00:06:46.982 --> 00:06:50.786
That noise is exactly what I'll be thinking
about when I try to go to sleep tonight.

00:06:50.786 --> 00:06:54.348
And I'll be dreaming about you sucking
out my eyes with your tentacle face,

00:06:54.348 --> 00:06:57.335
while I'm nestled up against a
stack of rotted corpses,

00:06:57.335 --> 00:07:00.553
then my intestines will burst
with insects crawling out of them,

00:07:00.553 --> 00:07:03.200
then the screaming--jeez,
that's a long drop.

00:07:04.187 --> 00:07:05.434
Uh huh.

00:07:08.239 --> 00:07:11.668
That's it. I'm going to order a
grappling hook when I'm get out of here.

00:07:11.668 --> 00:07:13.467
This is never going to happen again.

